The Deputy Country Director for Program (DCDP) supervises the entire program portfolio. The DCDP is responsible for defining program development and implementation strategies, and planning on the basis of the overall Country Strategy, in close cooperation with Country Director, including formulation of new project proposals and continuous improvement of program’s implementation and quality.

Together with the Country Director, the DCDP represents PIN to donors, partners, authorities and other stakeholders, ensuring that PIN is recognized for its field experience and models of action. The DCDP cooperates closely with Deputy Country Director for Systems and Operations (DCDSO) to contribute to continues improvement of support processes, with Head of Communication and Advocacy Department (HoCA) to generate evidence and formulate key messages to influence the positive changes, as well as with Head of Safety, Security and Access (HoSA). Internally, the DCDP contributes to a positive working environment for PIN staff and ensures that continuous improvements and Safeguarding is integrated in programming and functioning of organization.

