**People in Need** (PIN) is a Czech-based international non-governmental organization (NGO) that has provided humanitarian and development assistance across more than 20 countries since 1992. Today, PIN stands as one of the largest organizations of its kind in Central and Eastern Europe, supporting vulnerable communities in Asia, Africa, the Middle East, and Eastern Europe. PIN empowers civil society, advocates for human rights, and promotes social inclusion both at home and abroad.

## **About the role:**

The Deputy Country Director for Program (DCDP) supervises the entire program portfolio. The DCDP is responsible for defining program development and implementation strategies, and planning on the basis of the overall Country Strategy, in close cooperation with Country Director, including formulation of new project proposals and continuous improvement of program’s implementation and quality.

Together with the Country Director, the DCDP represents PIN to donors, partners, authorities and other stakeholders, ensuring that PIN is recognized for its field experience and models of action. The DCDP cooperates closely with Deputy Country Director for Systems and Operations (DCDSO) to contribute to continues improvement of support processes, with Head of Communication and Advocacy Department (HoCA) to generate evidence and formulate key messages to influence the positive changes, as well as with Head of Safety, Security and Access (HoSA). Internally, the DCDP contributes to a positive working environment for PIN staff and ensures that continuous improvements and Safeguarding is integrated in programming and functioning of organization.

**Internal relations:**

- The DCDP reports directly to the Country Director who provides direction and general supervision. The DCDP serves as the line manager for Program Area Operations Director, Head of Grants and Reporting, Head of Quality and Program Development, Partnership Manager, Program Manager, Resilience and Recovery Coordinator, overseeing the work on Data Management team and Finance andf Administrative Coordinators and works closely with the DCDSO, HoSSA, HoCA, as well as relevant HQ departments and regional management.

**External relations:**

- In coordination with the Country Director, DCDP represents PIN in national and international events, meetings with donors, government partners, international organisations, local and national partners, regional and local authorities, other agencies, clusters, coordination bodies, etc. DCDP is alternate representing PIN in HCT.

